### TopUp Wallet — TopUp.Api
### The saga service: starts a top-up, which debits the wallet, charges the
### (simulated) operator, and compensates (refunds) if the operator declines.
###
### This file talks to BOTH services: it creates + funds an account on Wallet.Api
### (:5001), then runs top-ups on TopUp.Api (:5002). Run top-to-bottom.
###
### Simulator decline rule (to exercise the compensation path):
###   amount whose cents = .13  -> operator declines -> saga refunds
###   phoneNumber containing "fail" -> declines

@wallet = http://localhost:5001
@topup  = http://localhost:5002
@contentType = application/json

### Health
GET {{topup}}/health

###
# @name createAccount
### Create a wallet account (on Wallet.Api) to top up from.
POST {{wallet}}/accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "ownerName": "Grace Hopper",
  "currency": "USD",
  "opening": 200
}

###
@accountId = {{createAccount.response.body.$.id}}

### --- HAPPY PATH ---
### Top up $5 to a normal number. Returns 202 + topUpId + fee.
### Async result: wallet debited $5, operator charged OK, saga Completed.
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "phoneNumber": "+8801711000000",
  "amount": 5,
  "idempotencyKey": "topup-happy-001"
}

### --- COMPENSATION PATH ---
### Top up $5.13 — the simulator DECLINES (cents = .13).
### Async result: wallet debited $5.13, operator declines, saga sends a refund,
### balance ends back where it was. Check the ledger below: debit then credit.
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "phoneNumber": "+8801711000000",
  "amount": 5.13,
  "idempotencyKey": "topup-decline-001"
}

### --- DECLINE via phone number ---
### Any phone containing "fail" is declined -> compensated the same way.
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "phoneNumber": "fail-0170000000",
  "amount": 7,
  "idempotencyKey": "topup-decline-002"
}

### --- PRICE CACHE ---
### Repeat the $5 amount — the fee is served from the Redis cache (cache-aside).
### Watch the TopUp.Api logs: first $5 call was a MISS, this one is a HIT.
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "phoneNumber": "+8801711000000",
  "amount": 5,
  "idempotencyKey": "topup-cache-001"
}

### --- RATE LIMIT ---
### Fire these back-to-back. The limit is 5 top-ups per account per minute, so
### after the cap you get HTTP 429. (The requests above already count toward it,
### so you may hit 429 before the 5th here — that's the shared window working.)
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+880171", "amount": 1, "idempotencyKey": "rl-1" }

###
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+880171", "amount": 1, "idempotencyKey": "rl-2" }

###
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+880171", "amount": 1, "idempotencyKey": "rl-3" }

###
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+880171", "amount": 1, "idempotencyKey": "rl-4" }

###
POST {{topup}}/topups
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+880171", "amount": 1, "idempotencyKey": "rl-5" }

### --- INSPECT RESULTS (on Wallet.Api) ---
### Balance after all the above.
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}

### Ledger — see each debit and the refund credits that undo the declines.
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions

### Audit trail (MongoDB).
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/audit
